[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048620017","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3048620017","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3048620017,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61tj_x","user":{"login":"francoisdlt","id":935800,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkzNTgwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/935800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt","html_url":"https://github.com/francoisdlt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/francoisdlt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T11:56:59Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T12:02:09Z","body":"you don't even need to instantiate the scenes. \nSimply `@exporting` the scenes is enough to trigger a broken dependency error when reopening the project","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3048620017/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141966876","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3141966876","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3141966876,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67Rpwc","user":{"login":"CodeSmith32","id":21373557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzczNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21373557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeSmith32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-01T02:36:50Z","updated_at":"2025-08-01T02:36:50Z","body":"This sounds like a recursive PackedScene reference error. Are you getting something like this in your editor console when you link the scenes up that way?\n\n```\nERROR: ... Circular reference to resource being saved found: 'res://...' will be null next time it's loaded.\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141966876/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3197784694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3197784694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3197784694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-mlJ2","user":{"login":"alexiosiko","id":67430469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NDMwNDY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67430469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko","html_url":"https://github.com/alexiosiko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexiosiko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T17:18:31Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T17:19:41Z","body":"Issue persists still\n\nMy work around is export the string path for the time being\n\n```gdscript\nextends Area2D\n\n@export var scene_path_from_scenes: String\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tconnect(\"body_entered\", _on_body_entered)\n\nfunc _on_body_entered(body: Node2D) -> void:\n\tif not body.is_in_group(\"Player\"):\n\t\treturn\n\tvar scene_path = \"res://scenes/\" + scene_path_from_scenes\n\tget_tree().change_scene_to_file(scene_path)\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3197784694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3198692857","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3198692857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3198692857,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-qC35","user":{"login":"CodeSmith32","id":21373557,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzczNTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21373557?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32","html_url":"https://github.com/CodeSmith32","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CodeSmith32/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T23:16:06Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T23:16:43Z","body":"(@AThousandShips I don't think this is a bug. I'm pretty sure this is expected behavior.)\n\n-----\n\n@alexiosiko / @lionet1224 Sorry if I wasn't clear. @alexiosiko has the answer. It's not just a workaround. (I'd recommend using @export_file though - see below)\n\nA PackedScene is just that. It's the entire scene - all the nodes and their properties - packed in a special format using a Dictionary.\n\nIf you have a PackedScene stored inside scene A that refers to scene B, and then try to store in scene B a PackedScene of scene A, an actual instantiation of that would literally be infinite in size. It's not possible, because, when scene B is serialized inside scene A, it would reach the property that holds scene A and start serializing it. At some point inside of that, it would reach the property holding scene B, and start serializing that, which again would eventually reach and serialize scene A again, recursively expanding forever:\n\n```\nScene A contains scene B, which contains scene A, which contains scene B, which contains scene A...\n```\n\nThat's why the error occurs and says `Circular reference`. It cannot be done. This is expected behavior.\n\nTherefore, as @alexiosiko pointed out, storing a string refrence to the scene instead is the correct solution, and not just a workaround.\n\nIf you don't like copy/pasting paths, though (which I agree is annoying), just use [`@export_file`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_exports.html#strings-as-paths) which lets you drag-and-drop files the same way PackedScenes does.\n\nPackedScenes are really only a minor 'preload' optimization. There *are* other conveniences to PackedScenes, though:\n- Automatic inspector drag-drop behavior (without explicitly indicating \".tscn\" as with @export_file)\n- Direct instantiability as opposed to needing to load the scene first\n\n-----\n\n@AThousandShips,\n\nWith that said, I honestly think it would be a lot more intuitive if PackedScenes instead were stored as plain path strings, and would auto preload when the scene were instantiated. This would both eliminate this problem altogether and also feel a lot more intuitive. People seem to think that's how this works, and I personally have no idea what the use is to copying the entire scene structure into another scene on game compile or startup (not sure when that happens), especially since I know of no way to create a custom PackedScenes for scenes that do not exist as files at some point in time.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3198692857/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3400786712","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3400786712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3400786712,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Ks-MY","user":{"login":"juniperajones","id":102542422,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhysVg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102542422?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones","html_url":"https://github.com/juniperajones","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juniperajones/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T08:52:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T19:35:05Z","body":"I recently experienced this problem without the recursive reference error. The packed scene simply returned null, with no further explanation.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3400786712/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419966928","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3419966928","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3419966928,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7L2I3Q","user":{"login":"cheyennix","id":47585766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NTg1NzY2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47585766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix","html_url":"https://github.com/cheyennix","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cheyennix/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-19T21:19:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T19:33:09Z","body":"_Bugsquad edit: Hidden as off-topic since the described issue does not match the issue from the MRP and this is a very long comment. Feel free to create an MRP for your issue and report it on its own._\n\n> I recently experienced this problem without the recursive reference error. The packed scene simply returned null, with no further explanation.\n\nI'm seconding this. There is no recursive reference. Except in my case, it's spawning the wrong scene entirely sometimes as well, and this is a huge issue.\n\nI'm getting this with a system I've made which I'll describe in case it's any help. It's a spawner class that's essentially a marker node which is placed within different scenes. It has a \"scene to spawn\" PackedScene export.\n\nThis node also has the possibility to be two different things, as an exported enum: A treasure spawner, which doesn't have an exported packedscene, and an object, which does have a set packed scene.\n\nBasically, the idea is just that if it's a treasure spawner, the dungeon tells the marker to spawn a randomly chosen treasure there, whereas if it's an object, the dungeon tells it to simply spawn it's exported packedscene.\n\nThe process:\n1. Dungeon gen takes a room data resource, which has a packed scene for the actual room node\n2. Dungeon spawns that room if possible, using that resource's packedscene\n3. That spawned room contains the various spawner markers which are configured properly.\n4. After the dungeon is generated, I call the spawn function on all of the markers, doing the right functionality based on their type.\n5. For some reason, the object ones come out mangled. Treasures spawn fine, and keep in mind that the packedscenes they spawn are generated on the fly, not using export-set ones. But the objects... it doesn't instantiate the correct scene that's set in the editor. It'll choose, seemingly arbitrarily, to duplicate one of the object scenes it chooses to spawn. Or, it'll say it's null in the debugger - yet printing what it is meant to spawn, and then what it has spawned, it has the correct packedscene set still, and yet it does not actually spawn the correct scene.\n\nI don't even know what's going on. I'm able to get around this by setting the spawner marker's packedscene export to a resource that has a reference to the packedscene, and that seems to work fine. Needless to say, that's an incredibly annoying workaround.\n\nThis has to be some weird cache thing with instantiating nodes or something, right?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419966928/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3960677852","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3960677852","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3960677852,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sEyXc","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T17:03:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T17:03:57Z","body":"We've tried to triage this during the Core meeting, and couldn't make perfect heads or tails of it but it sounds like this error might be expected due to cyclic references in how resources are loaded.\n\nWe're putting it in \"Up for grabs\" so we're inviting contributors to have a look and try to tackle it.\n\nIf members present in the meeting had it right, the best we can (but should!) do is improve error reporting for this kind of issue so users get a helpful error message that explains in detail what the problem is and how to solve it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3960677852/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961432683","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3961432683","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3961432683,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sHqpr","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T19:14:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T19:41:10Z","body":"This specific setup contains a cycle in the resource dependencies (scene 1 depends on scene 2 and scene 2 depends on scene 1). This is not supported for packed scenes and there are error messages regarding this:\n\n<img width=\"614\" height=\"394\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e63a615-fee0-4435-84a7-13b187982252\" />\n\n<img width=\"1190\" height=\"94\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/feacba8f-3d70-405d-87bc-23156a32837b\" />\n\nSo the only actionable thing in here would be to improve the error messaging. Some things that might be worth improving:\n- detecting the cycle when loading and adjust the error to specifically mention cyclic dependencies and not just \"dependency did not exist\" (also don't open the dependency fixer in editor for cycles)\n- correctly handle the returned error when loading the main scene. Currently we only check whether the returned resource is not null and ignore the error returned from the resource loader. At least some logging would be nice here.\n- document this somewhere? I could not find a direct documentation on cyclic dependencies not being supported. Maybe I did miss it. But it's actually pretty hard to say where this should even be documented. Given that cyclic dependency support is a per resource format loader thing.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961432683/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961440746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3961440746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3961440746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sHsnq","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T19:15:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T19:15:57Z","body":"There is meant to be an error when saving scenes with circular references but that might be broken as well, or it might just not have been noticed by the author of this issue","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961440746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961488259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3961488259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3961488259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sH4OD","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T19:24:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T19:24:18Z","body":"There is no error when creating this setup in the editor. If there was supposed to be one it certainly is not working.\n\nWe seem to have prevention measures for custom resources. When I try to create a similar setup with generic resources not with packed scenes I get this:\n\n<img width=\"442\" height=\"143\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec8fdcfd-3f95-4111-9760-9062e4d0a77a\" />\n\nBut it probably does not consider, that export properties of nodes become dependencies of the resulting packed scene.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961488259/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961509962","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3961509962","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3961509962,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sH9hK","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T19:28:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T19:28:10Z","body":"That part should absolutely be a bug of its own I'd say, the code in question is this:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/923c751af4e35fe8ef5f24d72333a561030f7382/scene/resources/resource_format_text.cpp#L1650-L1653\nfor text based files and this:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/923c751af4e35fe8ef5f24d72333a561030f7382/core/io/resource_format_binary.cpp#L2057-L2060\nfor binary ones","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3961509962/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3962465547","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3962465547","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3962465547,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sLm0L","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T22:22:48Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T22:22:48Z","body":"Do you actually have examples were this warning works? This feels like a pretty bad place to check for dependency cycles, given that it only searches for one \"layer\" of external dependencies and not the transitive hull of dependencies.\n\nOr differently: this check really only prevents cycles between builtin resources.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3962465547/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3962552629","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104769#issuecomment-3962552629","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104769","id":3962552629,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sL8E1","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_